1
00:00:00,998 --> 00:00:02,156
Welcome to Lumen.

2
00:00:02,156 --> 00:00:05,628
A friendly chat workspace, built on GitHub Copilot.

3
00:00:05,935 --> 00:00:09,514
You may already chat with GitHub Copilot in VS Code.

4
00:00:09,514 --> 00:00:13,850
Behind the scenes, that chat now runs on the Copilot CLI agent.

5
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:17,772
It reads your files, uses tools, and gets real work done.

6
00:00:17,772 --> 00:00:24,517
But VS Code is built around code, and most of the team works in plans, spreadsheets and documents.

7
00:00:24,838 --> 00:00:31,689
Lumen runs on that same Copilot agent, in a chat window built for that kind of work, on your own computer.

8
00:00:31,689 --> 00:00:35,889
And yes, if Claude Code is what you have, Lumen runs on that too.

9
00:00:36,154 --> 00:00:40,894
In the next few minutes, you'll learn how to use every part of it, step by step.

10
00:00:40,894 --> 00:00:42,139
Including what's new.

11
00:00:42,139 --> 00:00:49,722
Thirty nine specialist agents, more than seventy ready made prompts, sample projects for every discipline, and PowerPoint decks.

12
00:00:50,001 --> 00:00:50,663
Step one.

13
00:00:50,663 --> 00:00:51,473
Get set up.

14
00:00:53,486 --> 00:00:56,456
The first time you open Lumen, it asks three things.

15
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:57,027
Your name,

16
00:01:00,102 --> 00:01:01,626
which AI engine to use.

17
00:01:01,626 --> 00:01:05,734
GitHub Copilot is ready, and Claude Code sits right beside it,

18
00:01:08,861 --> 00:01:10,765
and where your work lives.

19
00:01:10,765 --> 00:01:12,888
That folder is your notebook.

20
00:01:12,888 --> 00:01:18,525
Keep it in OneDrive, and Microsoft 365 Copilot can find the same files later.

21
00:01:22,306 --> 00:01:22,888
Step two.

22
00:01:22,888 --> 00:01:24,247
Find your way around.

23
00:01:26,278 --> 00:01:31,122
If you've used Microsoft 365 Copilot, this will feel familiar.

24
00:01:31,122 --> 00:01:32,529
That's on purpose.

25
00:01:34,497 --> 00:01:36,133
The same rail on the left.

26
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:38,714
Chat, Agents, Prompts, and your Notebook.

27
00:01:38,714 --> 00:01:46,392
The same words, and the same habits, so everything you learn here carries straight over when your Copilot licence arrives.

28
00:01:46,392 --> 00:01:48,910
Below them, Lumen adds a few of its own.

29
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:52,246
Lifecycle runs, Insights, and Samples to practise on.

30
00:01:54,243 --> 00:02:00,835
And so nobody mixes them up, every message box says plainly which tool you're in, and which engine is answering.

31
00:02:01,815 --> 00:02:02,472
Step three.

32
00:02:02,472 --> 00:02:03,607
Chat with an agent.

33
00:02:04,533 --> 00:02:05,870
Agents are specialists.

34
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:10,869
Pick one, like the Requirements Coach, and it offers starter prompts to get you going.

35
00:02:12,666 --> 00:02:15,553
Under the message box, choose what Lumen may do.

36
00:02:15,553 --> 00:02:18,680
Just chat, read your files, or create and edit them.

37
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:21,626
And pick a response mode, from quick to thorough.

38
00:02:23,186 --> 00:02:27,047
Send it, and the answer streams in, with real headings and tables.

39
00:02:32,722 --> 00:02:39,548
User stories, Given, When, Then acceptance criteria, and the open questions to take back to the business.

40
00:02:40,731 --> 00:02:41,371
Step four.

41
00:02:41,371 --> 00:02:42,651
Work with the reply.

42
00:02:45,526 --> 00:02:47,172
Lumen suggests a next step.

43
00:02:47,172 --> 00:02:50,646
Click it to send, or press the up arrow to edit it first.

44
00:02:53,351 --> 00:02:57,447
Every reply can be copied, retried, or branched into a new chat.

45
00:02:57,447 --> 00:03:00,647
A thumbs up or down tells the team what's working.

46
00:03:01,525 --> 00:03:02,605
Need a document?

47
00:03:02,605 --> 00:03:05,980
Export the reply to Word, PowerPoint, or Markdown.

48
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:11,041
Every heading becomes a slide, and replies with tables export to Excel too.

49
00:03:11,041 --> 00:03:11,784
Here, Word.

50
00:03:11,784 --> 00:03:16,373
Real headings, lists, and tables, saved straight into your notebook.

51
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:24,943
Your own messages can be edited and resent, or saved as a prompt to reuse any time.

52
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:26,534
Step five.

53
00:03:26,534 --> 00:03:27,743
Bring in your files.

54
00:03:31,658 --> 00:03:34,292
To practise, open Samples on the left.

55
00:03:34,292 --> 00:03:38,381
There are five made up projects, one for each kind of work.

56
00:03:38,381 --> 00:03:39,490
Use the PM demo.

57
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:44,479
A Microsoft Project plan, with a budget, risks, and timesheets in Excel.

58
00:03:46,973 --> 00:03:51,725
Lumen switches to the sample folder, and the home screen offers its best prompts.

59
00:03:51,725 --> 00:03:55,187
Open the Notebook to see everything in your project folder.

60
00:04:02,573 --> 00:04:09,997
To use a file in a chat, type a slash, exactly like in Microsoft 365 Copilot, and pick it.

61
00:04:10,935 --> 00:04:14,967
Lumen reads the real plan, and you can watch every step as it works.

62
00:04:21,425 --> 00:04:22,037
Step six.

63
00:04:22,037 --> 00:04:23,601
Use the prompt gallery.

64
00:04:27,528 --> 00:04:32,635
The gallery now holds more than seventy saved prompts, in sixteen categories.

65
00:04:32,635 --> 00:04:37,610
Project plans, quality engineering, security, data, Azure DevOps, and more.

66
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:42,717
Each one asks a few simple questions, then hands the work to the right agent.

67
00:04:47,028 --> 00:04:48,720
Open the project health check.

68
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:52,047
Lumen has already picked the right plan from your notebook.

69
00:04:52,047 --> 00:04:52,724
Click Start.

70
00:05:06,163 --> 00:05:12,072
Red, amber or green, the critical path, slippage against the baseline, and who's over allocated.

71
00:05:13,035 --> 00:05:16,043
And any table copies straight into Excel or Outlook.

72
00:05:16,319 --> 00:05:17,082
Step seven.

73
00:05:17,082 --> 00:05:18,260
Put it on repeat.

74
00:05:23,362 --> 00:05:26,087
Open the prompt again, and choose Repeat.

75
00:05:26,087 --> 00:05:33,066
Daily, weekly, monthly, or every few minutes between two times, for a busy window like a cutover weekend.

76
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:35,458
This one is weekly, Mondays at nine.

77
00:05:41,193 --> 00:05:43,391
Scheduled prompts get their own tab.

78
00:05:43,391 --> 00:05:48,339
Lumen runs them while it's open, and leaves the result waiting as an unread chat.

79
00:05:49,324 --> 00:05:50,003
Step eight.

80
00:05:50,003 --> 00:05:52,225
Let Lumen update your files, safely.

81
00:05:58,578 --> 00:06:04,167
Update the plan reads this week's progress workbook, and applies it to the Microsoft Project plan.

82
00:06:05,696 --> 00:06:07,574
It never touches the original.

83
00:06:07,574 --> 00:06:12,331
It saves an updated copy, checks the schedule again, and lists every change.

84
00:06:22,862 --> 00:06:27,427
See changes shows exactly what moved, task by task, before and after.

85
00:06:30,167 --> 00:06:33,948
To create new files, switch the chat to Create and edit files.

86
00:06:33,948 --> 00:06:36,631
Ask for an Excel tracker with a Gantt chart,

87
00:06:39,824 --> 00:06:43,216
and there it is, colour coded and ready for the steering committee.

88
00:06:45,378 --> 00:06:46,032
Step nine.

89
00:06:46,032 --> 00:06:47,469
Create your own agent.

90
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:54,133
There are now thirty nine specialist agents.

91
00:06:54,133 --> 00:06:58,857
Search by name, by what they do, or by skill, and sort them however you like.

92
00:07:02,519 --> 00:07:03,905
Can't find the right one?

93
00:07:03,905 --> 00:07:04,793
Create your own.

94
00:07:04,793 --> 00:07:08,065
Describe what you need in one sentence, and click Draft it.

95
00:07:10,914 --> 00:07:16,370
Lumen fills in the same fields as Agent Builder in Microsoft 365 Copilot.

96
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:20,330
Name, description, instructions, and starter prompts.

97
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:23,544
It even switches on the right capabilities.

98
00:07:27,324 --> 00:07:32,338
Anything marked Lumen only runs on this computer, so you always know what will carry over.

99
00:07:34,658 --> 00:07:37,197
Create it, and pin your favourites to the sidebar.

100
00:07:47,582 --> 00:07:48,286
Step ten.

101
00:07:48,286 --> 00:07:49,929
Connect Azure DevOps.

102
00:07:55,709 --> 00:07:59,848
In Settings, under Connections, paste your organisation's address.

103
00:07:59,848 --> 00:08:05,053
Lumen signs in with your Azure account, or an access token that it keeps encrypted.

104
00:08:05,313 --> 00:08:09,537
Check the connection, then pick the project, the team, and the wikis to search.

105
00:08:14,738 --> 00:08:19,922
Now agents like the Backlog Helper can search and read your work items and wiki pages.

106
00:08:32,532 --> 00:08:36,275
And when an agent wants to change something, it only proposes.

107
00:08:36,275 --> 00:08:38,932
Switch the chat to Create and edit, and ask.

108
00:08:53,505 --> 00:08:57,686
The change arrives as an approval card, showing exactly what will be written.

109
00:08:57,949 --> 00:09:01,049
Nothing reaches Azure DevOps until you click Apply.

110
00:09:01,049 --> 00:09:05,608
Lumen checks that nobody changed it in the meantime, and records your name.

111
00:09:06,605 --> 00:09:07,431
Step eleven.

112
00:09:07,431 --> 00:09:09,634
Run a guided delivery lifecycle.

113
00:09:17,239 --> 00:09:20,510
The lifecycle sample sets up a program's documents.

114
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:27,628
Requirements and a project definition in Word, a solution blueprint, a data model, and a traceability workbook.

115
00:09:33,212 --> 00:09:37,543
The traceability check reads every layer, from business requirement to story.

116
00:09:47,063 --> 00:09:53,154
Coverage for every layer, stories that would build the wrong thing, broken links, and conflicting sources.

117
00:09:53,154 --> 00:09:55,682
Each one with a cell reference and an owner.

118
00:10:01,179 --> 00:10:03,652
For bigger work, start a lifecycle run.

119
00:10:03,652 --> 00:10:10,373
Requirements, functional design, technical design, and stories, with an approval gate between every stage.

120
00:10:10,636 --> 00:10:14,614
Name the run, choose the source documents, and start the first stage.

121
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:18,764
Each stage works in its own chat, and saves its output to your notebook.

122
00:10:48,368 --> 00:10:51,928
Before you sign off, run an advisory traceability check.

123
00:10:51,928 --> 00:10:54,597
It reports gaps, and never changes a file.

124
00:11:09,883 --> 00:11:10,714
Then approve.

125
00:11:10,714 --> 00:11:15,634
Your name and the time are stamped on the output, and the next stage unlocks.

126
00:11:15,634 --> 00:11:22,406
With Azure DevOps connected, an approved stage publishes to the wiki, or becomes work items, in one click.

127
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:29,008
And any approved stage saves as a Word document, in the program's own template when it has one.

128
00:11:31,649 --> 00:11:32,391
Step twelve.

129
00:11:32,391 --> 00:11:34,060
Try the specialist samples.

130
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:43,403
Beyond plans and requirements, the other samples cover data, security, and change and training.

131
00:11:43,403 --> 00:11:45,574
Each one comes with its own agents.

132
00:11:46,451 --> 00:11:47,644
Use the data sample.

133
00:11:47,644 --> 00:11:54,088
It has a source extract with data quality problems planted in it, and a data dictionary to check it against.

134
00:11:58,422 --> 00:11:59,580
Profile a dataset.

135
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:02,603
Pick the extract and the dictionary, and start.

136
00:12:14,103 --> 00:12:17,707
The Data Profiler reports exactly what the code found.

137
00:12:17,707 --> 00:12:21,911
Every column profiled, and every rule break, with example rows.

138
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:30,849
And the findings are saved as a report, with scripts to run the same checks again in the data platform.

139
00:12:31,852 --> 00:12:32,694
Step thirteen.

140
00:12:32,694 --> 00:12:33,836
See what's working.

141
00:12:37,677 --> 00:12:41,880
Every thumbs up and down lands in Insights, by agent and by prompt.

142
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:44,013
And it all stays on this computer.

143
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:46,257
Step fourteen.

144
00:12:46,257 --> 00:12:49,462
Take it to Microsoft 365 Copilot.

145
00:12:58,237 --> 00:13:01,679
When your Copilot licence arrives, export any agent.

146
00:13:01,679 --> 00:13:06,578
Paste it straight into Agent Builder, or hand IT a ready made app package.

147
00:13:10,645 --> 00:13:15,807
Your prompts export too, as plain text, ready to save in Copilot's prompt gallery.

148
00:13:19,862 --> 00:13:26,859
And every agent and skill exports into VS Code, so it works in GitHub Copilot Chat and Claude Code too.

149
00:13:30,341 --> 00:13:40,666
For developers, Engineering packs save the developer, test automation, and pipeline agents into a code repository, so the whole team works to the same standards.

150
00:13:41,589 --> 00:13:42,472
Step fifteen.

151
00:13:42,472 --> 00:13:43,423
Make it yours.

152
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,708
Lumen is pluggable.

153
00:13:48,708 --> 00:13:54,200
It runs on GitHub Copilot, or on Claude Code, and switching is one click in Settings.

154
00:13:55,099 --> 00:13:56,678
Light or dark, your choice.

155
00:14:00,776 --> 00:14:03,848
And press control slash, for every keyboard shortcut.

156
00:14:07,127 --> 00:14:07,604
Lumen.

157
00:14:07,604 --> 00:14:15,319
Built for GitHub Copilot, ready for Microsoft 365 Copilot, and friendly for everyone on the team.
